Step 1 — View the Patient table
USE HealtchareDatabse;
GO

SELECT TOP (10) *
FROM dbo.Patient;
GO

Explain:

SELECT = what data you want
* = all columns
FROM = which table
TOP (10) = show only first 10 records
dbo.Patient = Patient table inside the database
Step 2 — Show only important patient columns

Instead of displaying every column:

SELECT TOP (10)
    PatientID,
    FirstName,
    LastName,
    DateOfBirth,
    GenderIdentity,
    CountryOfBirth,
    Citizenship
FROM dbo.Patient;
GO

This is a very good example for teaching why we normally select specific columns instead of SELECT *.

You can explain:

“The Patient table contains many columns. If I only need basic patient demographic information, I can specify exactly which columns SQL should return.”

Step 3 — Find the different countries in the database
SELECT DISTINCT
    CountryOfBirth
FROM dbo.Patient
ORDER BY CountryOfBirth;
GO

Explain:

DISTINCT removes duplicate values.
Even though there are many patients, each country appears only once.
ORDER BY displays the countries alphabetically.

For example, instead of:

Canada
India
Canada
USA
India
Canada

you get:

Canada
India
USA
